# X3: an all-four reset with the heal, then the S2 quad smoke with timings: the warmup, one coding stream (the sequential engine,
# unchanged by the fix, so it is the control for the timings), four concurrent streams (the first packed-4 rounds), and
# tp_decode_bench 4-stream shapes: the steady rate per user with the tile-split all-reduce (128 extra reduce-scatter and gather
# pairs, plus slices and concats, per packed round). The product is data.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card exactness window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/exact and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image X0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; the first engine build 10-30 min; the smoke tests 5-12 min; the two bench shapes 8-20 min:
# 30-70 min in all (the smoke step limit is 210 min).
# Stop rule: soft. Read against the baselines of the unfixed image: coding decode_tok_s 35.66 (must not move: one-tile calls pass
# through the wrapper), and for the 4-live packed rounds the [PACKED-PHASE] lines of the S3a concurrent arm (trace_ms median 77.2,
# p10-p90 76.4-77.2; readback_ms median 32.7). The cost of the split is the increase in trace_ms plus readback_ms per round; the
# prediction is 3-6 ms (about 128 pairs at 30-50 us), and above 15 ms the next step is one reduce-scatter per tile with a single
# shared gather. Also read the [PINDIAG] tile-split line and that the concurrent4 texts are coherent.
# Proves: the price of the fix in round time and steady tok/s per user at four streams, and that the solo engine speed is untouched.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-exact-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4,bench
C2_BENCH_SHAPES=4x4096,4x32768
